WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.727 --> 00:00:03.411 line:90%
We're going to play a little game
called My First Time.

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:04.456 line:90%
Oh...

00:00:04.499 --> 00:00:06.551 line:90%
It sounds very saucy and invasive.

00:00:08.711 --> 00:00:11.285 line:90%
The first movie you ever saw was?

00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:13.507 line:90%
The big one that
sticks out in my head is,

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:15.095 line:90%
I remember,
going to see <i>Grease</i>.

00:00:15.227 --> 00:00:16.401 line:90%
-HOST: Yes.
-In the theater.

00:00:16.401 --> 00:00:19.829 line:10%
And I thought, "Well, that's it.
I need heels and tight pants."

00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:20.693 line:10%
(LAUGHING)

00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:22.409 line:90%
That's-- that was my take away.

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:25.578 line:90%
That, like, the music,
the relationships.

00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:28.234 line:90%
I was like, "I have to get me some
tight pants and heels."

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:31.277 line:90%
Me, too. I was like, to get a man,
I'm gonna have to change myself.

00:00:31.277 --> 00:00:33.626 line:90%
And that's-- that's why we're
here today. That's what we wanna

00:00:33.626 --> 00:00:34.702 line:90%
-...teach young women.
-HOST: Yeah.

00:00:34.702 --> 00:00:37.046 line:90%
The first R-rated movie
you ever saw?

00:00:37.046 --> 00:00:41.972 line:90%
I snuck downstairs while
my parents were watching <i>Carrie</i>.

00:00:42.304 --> 00:00:45.283 line:90%
We had doors that opened up,
so I hid behind a door

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:47.062 line:90%
and I was just watching <i>Carrie</i>

00:00:47.459 --> 00:00:49.489 line:90%
through a--
through the crack in the door.

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:51.643 line:90%
And I got real freaked out.

00:00:51.643 --> 00:00:54.898 line:90%
I was too scared
to go back upstairs,

00:00:54.923 --> 00:00:57.067 line:90%
so I just stayed there watching it.

00:00:57.292 --> 00:01:01.209 line:90%
And I watched the whole movie
and I just was quietly sobbing

00:01:01.357 --> 00:01:03.712 line:90%
behind the-- as my parents
were like, watching the movie.

00:01:03.712 --> 00:01:07.828 line:90%
The first movie that you related to
and had a real effect on you?

00:01:07.828 --> 00:01:09.762 line:90%
There something about,
<i>Planes, Trains and Automobiles</i>.

00:01:10.194 --> 00:01:14.685 line:90%
That I just remember feeling crazy
because I was laughing so hard

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.707 line:90%
and then the next second
I was crying

00:01:16.707 --> 00:01:19.191 line:90%
and then I would laugh again.
I was like, "I feel crazy."

00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:20.684 line:90%
"Those aren't pillows..."

00:01:21.323 --> 00:01:23.302 line:90%
That whole movie is perfect.
It's perfect.

00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:25.795 line:90%
When was the first time
you realized you were funny?

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.350 line:90%
My family is funny.
We sat around the...

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:32.044 line:90%
the kitchen table every night
and had dinner together.

00:01:32.044 --> 00:01:34.150 line:90%
And it was always kind of like,
who could...

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:36.541 line:90%
who-- and we were just
telling stories from the day,

00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:39.467 line:10%
but, like, I remember feeling
kind of, like, proud

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:42.196 line:10%
if I told a story from my day
and, like, everybody laughed.

00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:43.625 line:90%
What was it like the first time

00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:45.778 line:90%
the director called action
on <i>The Boss</i>?

00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:49.330 line:90%
Kind of crazy because
I was producing it as well

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.052 line:90%
and we kind of got sucked
into the vortex of...

00:01:52.884 --> 00:01:55.597 line:90%
of getting it, getting it started
and getting it going.

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:58.933 line:90%
I always have a weird word or phrase
that gets me into, like,

00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:00.204 line:90%
the character's voice.

00:02:00.707 --> 00:02:01.960 line:10%
And I didn't have it.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.509 line:10%
And I thought-- I remember looking
at Ben and going,

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:08.691 line:90%
"I don't-- I, I, I don't know
what she sounds like."

00:02:08.818 --> 00:02:11.763 line:90%
Then we did one take where
it finally felt like my...

00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:13.961 line:90%
I finally felt like I dropped
into it.

00:02:13.961 --> 00:02:17.121 line:90%
It's like, okay...
We're not gonna be--

00:02:17.531 --> 00:02:18.442 line:90%
It's gonna be okay.

00:02:18.442 --> 00:02:20.303 line:90%
Do you have a word now that you use?

00:02:20.303 --> 00:02:22.110 line:90%
Or did your character
just come to you?

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.107 line:90%
On certain days,
Ben would make me do her laugh

00:02:25.107 --> 00:02:26.382 line:90%
and she goes, like, "Ha!"

00:02:26.992 --> 00:02:29.630 line:90%
Which later Kristen Bell was always
like, "You sound like Alf".

00:02:29.826 --> 00:02:34.396 line:90%
What was the first time that you
remember thinking, "I'm successful"?

00:02:34.725 --> 00:02:39.376 line:90%
Every time I wrap anything, I'm--
there's a little-- there's a...

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:42.018 line:90%
probably seventy percent of me
that's like,

00:02:42.018 --> 00:02:45.863 line:90%
"Well... it was a good run.
I'll never work again."

00:02:45.863 --> 00:02:46.650 line:90%
HOST: (CHUCKLES)

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.573 line:90%
I mean just to my core,
I always am like,

00:02:50.117 --> 00:02:52.701 line:90%
"Well, I'll-- I'll go back
to Illinois and...

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.293 line:90%
probably, I don't know,
plant corn or something.

00:02:56.293 --> 00:02:58.255 line:90%
I just always think like,
"That's it."

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.062 line:90%
The fact that we were like, "We
should write stuff and make movies."

00:03:01.062 --> 00:03:01.904 line:90%
Yeah--

00:03:01.904 --> 00:03:03.986 line:90%
At some point somebody
should be like, "You're nuts."

00:03:03.986 --> 00:03:05.840 line:90%
-And look where we are.
-I know!

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.061 line:90%
HOST: It's amazing.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.100 line:90%
Thank you so much,
Melissa, for sharing

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.539 line:90%
-your first time with me.
-Thank you.

00:03:10.539 --> 00:03:11.731 line:90%
-Yes.
-I appreciate it.

00:03:11.731 --> 00:03:12.803 line:90%
I'll never forget it.

00:03:12.803 --> 00:03:13.897 line:90%
HOST: (LAUGHS)

